 "This file can't be read. Use an Excel file (.xlsx) or a CSV file.": "Dan il-fajl ma jistax jinqara. Uża fajl Excel (.xlsx) jew fajl CSV.",
 "Import from": "Importa minn",
 "Spreadsheet": "Spreadsheet",
 "Can't read file": "Il-fajl ma jistax jinqara",
 "Choose file": "Agħżel fajl",
 "Excel or CSV": "Excel jew CSV",
 "One row per training day with a date column and a column per exercise, e.g. “Date | Leg press | Chest press” with “45”, “27 (3×10)” or “25 / 18” in the cells. A file with one row per set (date, exercise, reps, weight) works too, as does a Liftr export.": "Ringiela waħda għal kull jum ta' taħriġ b'kolonna tad-data u kolonna għal kull eżerċizzju, eż. “Data | Leg press | Chest press” b'“45”, “27 (3×10)” jew “25 / 18” fiċ-ċelloli. Taħdem ukoll fajl b'ringiela waħda għal kull sett (data, eżerċizzju, ripetizzjonijiet, piż), kif ukoll esportazzjoni minn Liftr.",
 "Imported workouts go into your history and charts, but are not written to Apple Health.": "It-taħriġ importat jidħol fl-istorja u fil-graffs tiegħek, imma ma jinkitibx f'Apple Health.",
 "Sheet": "Folja",
 "Sets per weight": "Settijiet għal kull piż",
 "Reps per set": "Ripetizzjonijiet għal kull sett",
 "Used when a cell only holds a weight. A cell like “27 (3×10)” keeps its own sets and reps.": "Jintuża meta ċellola jkun fiha biss piż. Ċellola bħal “27 (3×10)” żżomm is-settijiet u r-ripetizzjonijiet tagħha stess.",
 "Rename a column to link it to an exercise you already have.": "Biddel isem kolonna biex tgħaqqadha ma' eżerċizzju li diġà għandek.",
